## Native work and layout proof

Ordinary parsing, preparation, rewritten queries, reused prepared execution, SHACL parameter substitution, and native evaluation select static false/unit modes. There is no ordinary contextual policy allocation, context compiler, new whole-query census, row-delivery callback/storage, witness limit, retry scan, or per-row context initialization. The new boxed policy keeps existing enum sizes and tags; Apply and VarPairs are appended so old discriminant arithmetic and payload offsets remain stable. `PreparedRdflibQuery` storage accounting includes its own wrapper and saturating projection-name heap bytes without changing ordinary `PreparedQuery` representation.

The unit dispatcher uses the original native default attribute and one shared bare direct-argument match. Its contextual boundary and Apply kernel are genuinely out of line. Earlier emitted regressions were discovered and repaired: an explicit native noinline boundary retained an external sret ABI/live recursive frame; a captured match closure added storage/load/caller frame; an inline Apply group body enlarged the main dispatcher. All failed attempts remain in distinct historical artifact directories. Final attribution examines actual MAIN and LIBRARY homes independently: MAIN has restored one save/sub144/CFA160 and ordinary tail transfers; LIBRARY is compared to its own two-save/sub312/CFA336 baseline. Equal frame sizes or allocator logs alone are not treated as proof.

Native LATERAL caches prefix width once as before, and its inline helper takes that width explicitly. Unit correlation and substitution remove the typed input mask/consumer/Option machinery at specialization. Native Join/Minus invoke original algorithms; extracted Filter/Extend/Project/Graph/Group helpers preserve ordinary iteration, ownership, allocation, and drop scope and inline away. Group's native unit domain calls the unchanged shared-blank `visible_columns` loop; the source still handles hidden blank columns before COUNT(DISTINCT *). The moved mutable-expression walker is one unchanged body, not a forwarding runtime layer or second walker. Native false clone mapping has no callback ABI or call, and old-node clone/drop/hash/walk arms preserve their existing operations.

Final paired native evidence uses the identical original Rust probe in `raw/native-cost-probe` and `raw/native-cost-base-ir-probe` against the exact synchronized base. Eleven ordinary query shapes, eleven actual request-substitution windows, and three configured property-function workloads have byte-identical allocation counts/bytes, drop counts, retained bytes, layout, row counts, and metered resource vectors: `raw/t1-native-cost-base-863c75-extended.log` versus `raw/t1-native-cost-candidate-863c75-thin-apply.log` (`cmp` exit0). Layout is GraphPattern144/Expression64/Query264/PreparedQuery368/NodeRef16; EvalCtx944 in attributed ABI. This includes fixed/variable GRAPH, native LATERAL, Group, COUNT DISTINCT star, relation interception, and reuse, but does not pretend the IRI probe alone covers hidden-blank or SHACL semantics; those also have the existing core/actual SHACL controls and exact source/compiled argument.

Exact build: `cargo rustc --offline --release --manifest-path <owned-probe>/Cargo.toml --bin qualification-454-native-cost -vv -- --emit=llvm-ir,asm`. Effective wrapper-selected flags are opt3, thin LTO, codegen-units1, strip=symbols, `-D warnings`, target-cpu=native. `raw/t1-final-source-identity.log` records actual rustc/LLVM, and emitted modules pin CPU znver5/features/ABI. Probe manifest profile spelling is not substituted for actual flags. Build receipts are `raw/t1-synchronized-{base-863c75-extended,candidate-863c75-thin-apply}-ir-build.log`. Final complete unmodified main/eval/algebra modules are `raw/native-cost-base-863c75-extended-ir` and `raw/native-cost-candidate-863c75-thin-apply-ir`; full original function/assembly sections and attributable inventories have corresponding `-sections` and `t1-native-cost-*-inventory.log` names. Calls, branches, loads, byte offsets, spills, and cleanup are retained.

Existing ordinary governor profile charges/trip points are unchanged: ordinary source charge/checkpoint sequence is preserved, exhaustive native soundness controls pass, and paired metered resource vectors are identical. New contextual primitive classification is certified independently; it does not change an existing native profile operation, so no governor profile version is bumped.

The independent native-cost report `tasks/T1-native-cost-review.md` gives final disposition MET at this frozen source, including false clone callback erasure, identical old-node drop dispatch/layout, moved expression-walk caller attribution, native hidden-blank group visibility, and main/library frames/tails. The independent law report `tasks/T1-review.md` gives final PASS at the same 37-file manifest. No performance guarantee is manufactured from a rare branch, equal allocator totals, symbol absence, elapsed host timing, or an uninspected compiler assumption.

